      "hi": "According to Color Code rules (BBROYGBVGW): Blue = 6, Grey = 8, Red = multiplier 10^2 (100). That means basic value = 68 * 100 = 6800 Ohm. Silver color tolerance = ±10%. 10% of 6800 = 680 Ohm. Minimum Value = 6800 - 680 = 6460 Ohm. So option D is correct.",
      "kn": "According to Color Code rules (BBROYGBVGW): Blue = 6, Grey = 8, Red = multiplier 10^2 (100). That means basic value = 68 * 100 = 6800 Ohm. Silver color tolerance = ±10%. 10% of 6800 = 680 Ohm. Minimum Value = 6800 - 680 = 6460 Ohm. So option D is correct.",
      "te": "According to Color Code rules (BBROYGBVGW): Blue = 6, Grey = 8, Red = multiplier 10^2 (100). That means basic value = 68 * 100 = 6800 Ohm. Silver color tolerance = ±10%. 10% of 6800 = 680 Ohm. Minimum Value = 6800 - 680 = 6460 Ohm. So option D is correct.",
      "ta": "According to Color Code rules (BBROYGBVGW): Blue = 6, Grey = 8, Red = multiplier 10^2 (100). That means basic value = 68 * 100 = 6800 Ohm. Silver color tolerance = ±10%. 10% of 6800 = 680 Ohm. Minimum Value = 6800 - 680 = 6460 Ohm. So option D is correct.",
